# Direct hosting (no Cloudflare): https://3d-avatar.novaeuropa.space with Caddy's own certificates.
#
# Caddy runs as an unprivileged user service inside WSL2, which may not bind ports below 1024,
# so it listens on 8080/8443. Windows forwards the public ports to them (deploy/windows/):
#     internet :80  -> router -> Windows :80  -> WSL :8080   (ACME HTTP-01 + redirect to HTTPS)
#     internet :443 -> router -> Windows :443 -> WSL :8443   (the site)
# Caddy assumes the public ports are 80/443, so certificates and redirects work unchanged.
# Environment (set by the systemd unit): SITE_ROOT, LOG_DIR.
{
	http_port 8080
	https_port 8443

	servers {
		# Windows' port forwarding is TCP-only; advertising HTTP/3 (UDP) would make browsers
		# try a path that can't connect.
		protocols h1 h2
	}

	# Optional: ACME account contact (Let's Encrypt no longer sends expiry mail; not required).
	# email you@example.com
}

3d-avatar.novaeuropa.space {
	import site.caddy
}
